function.description:
Read the contents of a text file within the workspace. Returns the file contents as a string. Files must be within the workspace directory (or, read-only, /tmp) and under 10MB. Optionally provide start_line and end_line (1-based, inclusive) to read a specific range. Without an end_line, up to 2000 lines are returned. Every read is capped at ~20,000 characters, cut on a line boundary; when a read is truncated, the output includes returned_start_line / returned_end_line plus next_start_line so you can continue with another ranged read. For large documentation or data tasks, prefer targeted ranges, search, profile_data, describe_data, or query_data instead of reading whole files. For binary files (images, PDFs), use read_binary instead.

Examples:
- Read source code: {"path": "src/main.rs"}
- Read config: {"path": "config.json"}
- Read nested file: {"path": "src/utils/helpers.rs"}
- Read a range: {"path": "src/main.rs", "start_line": 40, "end_line": 80}

List the contents of a directory within the workspace. Returns file and directory names with type and size metadata. Results are sorted with directories first, then files alphabetically.

Examples:
- List workspace root: {"path": "."}
- List subdirectory: {"path": "src"}
- List nested directory: {"path": "src/components"}

Search for files matching a glob pattern within the workspace. Returns matching file paths relative to the workspace root. Results are limited to 1000 matches.

Pattern syntax:
- `*` matches any sequence of characters in a file/dir name
- `**` matches any number of directories (recursive)
- `?` matches a single character
- `[abc]` matches one of the characters

Examples:
- Find all Rust files: {"pattern": "**/*.rs"}
- Find all test files: {"pattern": "**/test_*.py"}
- Find configs: {"pattern": "*.{json,toml,yaml}"}

Search for a text pattern or regex in the workspace using ripgrep. Returns matching lines with file paths and line numbers. Requires 'rg' (ripgrep) to be installed. Results are limited to max_results (default 100).

Examples:
- Search for a function: {"pattern": "fn main"}
- Case-insensitive search: {"pattern": "TODO", "case_insensitive": true}
- Search only Rust files: {"pattern": "use std", "file_type": "rust"}
- Search only Python files: {"pattern": "def main", "file_type": "py"}
- Limit results: {"pattern": "error", "max_results": 20}
